{"episodes":{"191268":"A thunderstorm on the east side of Tucson produced a wind gust strong enough to uproot a large Palo Verde tree.","191314":"Widespread thunderstorms impacted the Tucson Metro on the afternoon of June 28th. Some of these storms resulted in severe threshold wind gusts.","191553":"A supercell moved across parts of Lyon and Osage Counties on the evening of June 28. This storm produced three brief tornadoes,  as well as flash flooding and a larger area of scattered 70-85 mph straight-line winds.","192031":"An unstable southwest flow aloft was over the Billings Forecast Area. Large-scale ascent ahead of a midlevel trough tracked eastward across the northern Rockies. Thunderstorms developed over the mountains of southwest Montana and moved east onto the adjacent plains. Wind shear of around 50kts supported storm organization resulting in organized thunderstorm clusters and supercells, some of which produced large hail and severe outflow winds.","192082":"Thunderstorms moving offshore produced a strong wind gust in Fort Pierce.","192523":"A couple of discrete severe storms impacted the central to southern Texas Panhandle on the evening of the 25th producing damaging winds and one instance of 1\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd hail.  On the 26th, some more discrete severe storms, this time embedded in some widespread thunderstorm activity across the western combined Panhandles produced damaging winds with one instance of hail up to 1\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd in diameter. Then on the 27th a line of storms moved in from southeastern Colorado produced hail up to 1\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd in diameter in Texas County in the OK Panhandle and a wind gust up to 64 mph in Lipscomb County the far northeastern TX Panhandle.","192524":"A couple of discrete severe storms impacted the central to southern Texas Panhandle on the evening of the 25th producing damaging winds and one instance of 1\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd hail.  On the 26th, some more discrete severe storms, this time embedded in some widespread thunderstorm activity across the western combined Panhandles produced damaging winds with one instance of hail up to 1\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd in diameter. Then on the 27th a line of storms moved in from southeastern Colorado produced hail up to 1\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd in diameter in Texas County in the OK Panhandle and a wind gust up to 64 mph in Lipscomb County the far northeastern TX Panhandle.","192608":"A slowly decaying complex of thunderstorms moved from south-central Kansas into northern Oklahoma during the early morning of the 28th. Despite the intensity trend (downward), a few severe-caliber wind gusts were measured by surface observing platforms across the area.","192675":"A line of storms moved across central South Dakota during the late evening and early overnight hours. The storms mainly generated strong winds, with observed gusts as high as 74 mph. These thunderstorm winds were responsible for damaging a pole barn located 1 mile south of Highmore. Additionally, a farmer later indicated that a tornado had touched down in an open field, which was confirmed by satellite data.","192856":"A frontal boundary had stalled across south Louisiana. Scattered thunderstorms developed along this front but a weak steering pattern resulted in slow moving storms. One of these storms produced heavy rain over St Bernard parish which resulted in flash flooding.","193010":"Prevailing SW flow over a moist and unstable airmass triggered strong to pulse severe storms toward the Atlantic coast where sea breeze and boundary mergers occurred.","193011":"Prevailing SW flow over a moist and unstable airmass triggered strong to pulse severe storms toward the Atlantic coast where sea breeze and boundary mergers occurred.","193013":"Prevailing SW flow over a moist and unstable airmass triggered strong to pulse severe storms toward the Atlantic coast where sea breeze and boundary mergers occurred.","193098":"Wind on 06/27.","193099":"Heavy rain and flooding on 06/28.","193308":"Thunderstorms developed as surface low pressure deepened over eastern Montana and a warm front lifted through North Dakota. The main threat from the storms was damaging winds, with the strongest winds of 90 mph occurring in Stark County. Buildings, trees, and crops were damaged. Two tornadoes were reported, with one near Trotters in Golden Valley County and the other near South Heart in Stark County. Both tornadoes occurred in open fields with no damage to evaluate, and so were rated EFU (Unknown) by National Weather Service policy. Although damaging winds were the main threat, some large hail did occur. The largest hail was the size of ping pong balls, and fell in Stark County.","193377":"Deep monsoon moisture lead to a few severe thunderstorms across northern Arizona.","193398":"A line of strong to severe thunderstorms developed over northwest South Dakota and tracked eastward across much of the area. The storms produced wind gusts of 60 to near 90 mph in some areas.","193438":"Mid-level shortwave energy advancing into the area and encountering an environment displaying modest instability and strong downdraft CAPE led to thunderstorms capable of producing damaging wind gusts across coastal waters.","193703":"Heavy rain sat over a sections of Calcasieu, Vermilion, Cameron, and Jefferson Davis parishes during the early morning hours of the 28th.","193721":"Severe thunderstorms brought heavy rain, hail, gusty winds, and flash flooding.","193859":"Lingering sub-tropical moisture remained in place with drier air moving in from the west as a low pressure trough passed though. This resulted in sufficient shear across northwest Colorado where some storms produced up to penny size hail that covered Highway 13.","193926":"An unstable environment with better shear produced isolated strong to severe thunderstorms. Wind damage was reported near Canon City.","194790":"Lingering sub-tropical moisture remained in place with drier air moving in from the west as a low pressure trough passed though. Sufficient shear and enough moisture remained in place to allow for a few strong storms, one of which produced heavy rain rates over Gunnison County to result in debris flows in an area of steep terrain."},"events":[{"begin":"2024-06-28T00:02Z","county":"Stark","damageCrops":"75.00K","damageProperty":"100.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2024-06-28T00:05Z","endLat":46.68,"endLon":-103.2,"episode":193308,"id":1194789,"injuries":0,"lat":46.68,"location":"13.82 S Belfield","lon":-103.2,"magnitude":1.5,"narrative":"Hail combined with wind to dent tin on building roofs and shred window screens. In addition, crops were also damaged.","source":"Public","state":"ND","type":"Hail","wfo":"BIS"},{"begin":"2024-06-28T00:10Z","county":"Bowman","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2024-06-28T00:12Z","endLat":46.17,"endLon":-103.3,"episode":193308,"id":1194790,"injuries":0,"lat":46.17,"location":"3.35 W Buffalo Spgs","lon":-103.3,"magnitude":59.0,"magnitudeType":"MG","source":"AWOS","state":"ND","type":"Thunderstorm Wind","wfo":"BIS"},{"begin":"2024-06-28T00:12Z","county":"Harding","damageCrops":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2024-06-28T00:20Z","endLat":45.6,"endLon":-103.55,"episode":193398,"id":1194871,"injuries":0,"lat":45.6,"location":"(2Wx)Buffalo","lon":-103.55,"magnitude":79.0,"magnitudeType":"MG","source":"ASOS","state":"SD","type":"Thunderstorm Wind","wfo":"UNR"},{"begin":"2024-06-28T00:18Z","county":"Harding","damageCrops":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2024-06-28T00:18Z","endLat":45.38,"endLon":-103.55,"episode":193398,"id":1194872,"injuries":0,"lat":45.38,"location":"7.6 N Redig","lon":-103.55,"magnitude":52.0,"magnitudeType":"MG","source":"Mesonet","state":"SD","type":"Thunderstorm Wind","wfo":"UNR"},{"begin":"2024-06-28T00:20Z","county":"Billings","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2024-06-28T00:22Z","endLat":46.9,"endLon":-103.29,"episode":193308,"id":1194791,"injuries":0,"lat":46.9,"location":"2.51 NE Fryburg","lon":-